			"61": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "XY OSCILLOSCOPE\n\nAre you ready to get your Sine buzzin' ?\nIn this example we are using the Mesh2D system to create an oscilloscope that exists out of a thousand little dots.\n\nTo start off you should have a good play around with the parameters, because it is simply fun to play around with this patch. Maybe even render out a clip! Did you even know that that is possible!?\n\nNext you should have a play with the post-processing stuff at the end of the patch; adjust the grid, vignetting, and distortion. Make it prettier than we did, or just mess it up and reload the patch.. we'll pretend it never happened.\n\nIn this example we are using Sine oscillators, but you could switch them out for any oscillator you like. In fact, we encourage you to do so! There is even the option to go to the next level and enter the realm of waveshaping by multiplying oscillators with each other. You could also get real funky and introduce audio using the Spectrum node."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 300.94873046875,
					"width": 657.3099365234375,
					"x": -789.16876220703125,
					"y": -73.1974639892578125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"66": {
				"attributes": {
					"instances": {
						"type": "integer",
