			"71": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "POST-PROCESSING\n\nWe start creating the oscilloscope look by introducing a little bit of static in the system.\nNext we take our crisp texture and use a Blur node to blur it.\nWe create a Grid for the background with a Grid node.\nA second Grid node is used to create some scanlines by using the Slide node to move it.\nTo get a bit of distortion going we use the scanlines to UV Offset the whole patch\nFinally we apply some vignetting to get a CRT-look going."
					}
				},
